                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>At its meeting held on March 4, 1954, the National Security Council considered
                    and adopted the draft statement of policy contained in NSC 5409, “United States
                    Policy Toward South Asia,” dated February 19, 1954, subject to certain
                    alterations. On March 6, President Eisenhower approved NSC 5409 as amended.
                    Section D of NSC 5409 deals specifically with Afghanistan.</p>
                <p>For texts of NSC 5409, Gleasion’s memorandum (drawn up March 5) of the NSC
                    discussion on March 4, and Section D of NSC 5409, see pages 1089, 1126, and
                    1151, respectively.</p>
            </div>
